From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:43:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: describe the
 camera module EEPROMs

Both camera modules carry an EEPROM with their calibration data on the
camera I2C bus: the rear one at 0x58 on the module's 2.8 V AF rail, the
front one at 0x51 on its 2.8 V analog rail, both with 16-bit offsets.
The bus pull-ups hang on the modules' 1.8 V I/O rail. Describe them as
read-only 24c32 with both rails, as the vendor tree powers them, so that
the data can be read through nvmem; nothing writes them.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts    | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 3ff002f3c54c..a2416ee0482d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1327,6 +1327,28 @@
 			};
 		};
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The camera modules' EEPROMs (calibration data), 16-bit offsets, never
+	 * written: front (stock module data: address 0xa2 in 8-bit form) and
+	 * rear (stock "qcom,eeprom0"), each on its module's 2.8 V rail. The
+	 * pull-ups of this bus hang on the modules' 1.8 V I/O rail.
+	 */
+	eeprom@51 {
+		compatible = "atmel,24c32";
+		reg = <0x51>;
+		vcc-supply = <&vreg_l14b_2p8>;
+		vio-supply = <&vreg_l2f_1p8>;
+		read-only;
+	};
+
+	eeprom@58 {
+		compatible = "atmel,24c32";
+		reg = <0x58>;
+		vcc-supply = <&vreg_l16b_2p8>;
+		vio-supply = <&vreg_l2f_1p8>;
+		read-only;
+	};
 };
 
 /* stock drives the camera bus with 8 mA (qupv3_se9_i2c_sda_active / _scl_active) */
